# Small-system (8 atoms) LAMMPS ground truth for cross-validating exaStamp's new
# compute_descriptor_pod_global against real LAMMPS compute pod/global. Unlike pod/atom or
# podd/atom, this compute produces a GLOBAL ARRAY (not a per-atom quantity), which can't be
# exported with an ordinary `dump` command -- instead every element is printed explicitly via
# LAMMPS's immediate-variable c_ID[i][j] syntax. Rows/cols (25 x 32) are specific to this fixed
# 8-atom Ta_small system + Ta_param.pod (Mdesc=31, nl1=1, nelements=1 -> nCoeffAll=32,
# 1+3*8=25 rows) -- generated once (not a general-purpose loop) since both dimensions are fixed
# and known in advance for this test config, matching how other LAMMPS scripts in this test dir
# already hardcode config-specific values (e.g. in.pod_descriptors's element-name argument).

units       metal
atom_style  atomic
boundary    p p p

read_data   Ta_small.lmp

pair_style  zero 5.01
pair_coeff  * *

compute podg all pod/global Ta_param.pod Ta_coefficients.pod Ta

run         0

